<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bera, Count of Barcelona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 844</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bera was the first count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> captured the city in 801, a Goth probably descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-of-gellone">William of Gellone</a>. Accused of treason and of dealings with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, he lost a judicial duel at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a> in 820 and was deposed and exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a>, where he died. His fall left the Spanish March to Frankish counts and, later, to the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-barcelona">House of Barcelona</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bera-count-of-barcelona.jpg" alt="Bera, Count of Barcelona" width="320" height="571" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bera.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
